menu "Steam2Switch2 adapter"

    config S2S_SC2_MAC
        string "Steam Controller 2 MAC address(es)"
        default ""
        help
            Optional allowlist of BLE addresses, comma/space separated, e.g.
            "c1:2a:3b:4c:5d:6e" or "c1:2a:3b:4c:5d:6e, d4:11:22:33:44:55".

            A device whose address matches is accepted even if it does not
            advertise a "Steam" name and does not advertise the Valve service
            UUID. Left empty, matching falls back to name + Valve service only.
            Consumed by the Steam Controller 2 central (sc2_central.cpp).

    config S2S_SC2_MAC_ONLY
        bool "Connect ONLY to the configured MAC address(es)"
        default n
        help
            Ignore name / Valve-service matching entirely and accept only the
            addresses in S2S_SC2_MAC. Use this once the controller's address is
            known, so no other Steam-named device can be picked up by mistake.

    config S2S_WEB_ENABLE
        bool "Enable the macro editor web UI (Wi-Fi access point)"
        default y
        help
            Serves the macro editor from the adapter over its own Wi-Fi access
            point. Wi-Fi and Bluetooth share the radio, so enabling this adds
            coexistence traffic; disable it for the lowest possible input
            latency when macros are not needed.

    config S2S_WIFI_SSID
        string "Access point name"
        default "Puck2Switch2"
        depends on S2S_WEB_ENABLE

    config S2S_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Access point password (empty = open network)"
        default ""
        depends on S2S_WEB_ENABLE
        help
            At least 8 characters enables WPA2. Leave empty for an open network,
            which is the easiest to join from a phone or laptop.

endmenu
